Spring Boot + PostgreSQL + Docker (Multi-Container Project)

This project demonstrates a Spring Boot REST API running inside Docker and connected to a PostgreSQL database using Docker Compose (multi-container setup).

🚀 Tech Stack

Java 17

Spring Boot

Spring Web

Spring Data JPA

PostgreSQL

Maven

Docker

Docker Compose

📁 Project Structure
strudent/
│
├── src/
│   └── main/java/com/docker/strudent/
│       ├── StrudentApplication.java
│       ├── Student.java
│       └── StudentController.java
│
├── Dockerfile
├── docker-compose.yml
├── pom.xml
└── README.md
⚙️ How It Works

Architecture:

Browser → localhost:8080
        ↓
Spring Boot Container (app)
        ↓
PostgreSQL Container (db)

The app container runs the Spring Boot application.

The db container runs PostgreSQL.

Docker Compose manages both services.

🐳 Docker Setup
1️⃣ Dockerfile
FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jdk
WORKDIR /app
COPY target/*.jar app.jar
ENTRYPOINT ["java","-jar","app.jar"]
2️⃣ docker-compose.yml
version: '3.8'

services:
  db:
    image: postgres:15
    container_name: postgres-db
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: studentdb
      POSTGRES_USER: postgres
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: password
    ports:
      - "5432:5432"

  app:
    build: .
    container_name: spring-app
    ports:
      - "8080:8080"
    depends_on:
      - db
🛠️ Build and Run
Step 1: Build the JAR file
mvn clean package

Make sure you see:

BUILD SUCCESS
Step 2: Start Containers
docker compose up --build

Wait until you see:

Tomcat started on port 8080
Started StrudentApplication
🌐 API Endpoint

Open in browser:

http://localhost:8080/students
Sample Response
[
  {"id":1,"name":"ram","age":22},
  {"id":2,"name":"jhon","age":26},
  {"id":3,"name":"Alice","age":18}
]
Test with Curl
curl http://localhost:8080/students

Stop Containers
docker compose down

To remove volumes:

docker compose down -v